<!-- ============ 9 · SMART NEBULIZERS ============ -->
<section id="ch40-smart">
  <div class="sec-head"><div class="sec-no">09</div><div>
    <h2>Smart nebulizers — and the drug–device combinations</h2>
    <p>Nebulizers that watch how you breathe and decide when to puff.</p>
    <p><span class="chip">Slides 35–36, 39</span></p>
  </div></div>

  <div class="grid g2">
    <div class="pop"><figure><img class="tilt" src="data:image/jpeg;base64," alt="Vibrating mesh smart nebulizer"/>
    <figcaption><p class="anchor"><b>Memory anchor:</b> The I-neb watches your first three breaths, then puffs drug over <span class="num rv">50%</span> of each inspiration — the nebulizer that learns how you breathe.</p></figcaption></figure></div>
    <div class="stack">
      <div class="card">
        <h3>🧠 I-neb (slide 35)</h3>
        <p><b>I-neb (Philips Respironics):</b> a breath-actuated passive vibrating mesh nebulizer with <b>adaptive aerosol delivery</b> — it monitors pressure changes and inspiratory time for the patient's <b>first three consecutive breaths</b>; drug is aerosolized over <b><span class="num rv">50%</span> of the inspiratory maneuver</b> during the fourth and subsequent breaths. Released for delivery of <b>prostacyclin</b>.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>🎛️ Akita, Fox, Dance 501 (slide 36)</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><b>Akita (Activaero):</b> controls inspiratory flow to keep it slow (<b><span class="num rv">12–15 L/min</span></b>) and reduce impaction loss in the upper airways. Patient pulmonary function is stored on a <b>smart card</b> programmed to tell the device when to generate aerosol during inhalation.</li>
          <li><b>Fox:</b> active vibrating mesh nebulizer with a flow- and volume-controlled inhalation system that increases intrapulmonary deposition.</li>
          <li><b>Dance 501:</b> investigational — the deck gives no further detail.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>💊 Drug–device combinations (slide 39)</h3>
        <p>The deck's title for this slide carries a typo — <b>"Combinatins"</b> — and the slide names four entries with no further detail. Taught as written:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Lonhana Magnair</li>
          <li>Tyvaso</li>
          <li>Cayston, Altera eFlow</li>
          <li>Staccato</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
