      <li><b>Aerosol =</b> particles in gas. <b>Emitted → inhaled → respirable:</b> only a fraction survives each step.</li>
      <li><b>MMAD:</b> cascade impaction; <b>VMD:</b> laser diffraction; <b>GSD:</b> wider = more mixed.</li>
      <li><b>Impaction &gt;5 µm; sedimentation 1–5 µm; diffusion &lt;3 µm.</b> Hold your breath — sedimentation needs time; <b>0.5–1 µm</b> mostly exhales.</li>
      <li><b>Targets:</b> upper 5–&gt;50 µm; lower 2–5 µm; alveoli 1–3 µm. (The deck lists parenchyma twice — the second listing is &lt;0.1 µm.)</li>
