<!-- ============ MEMORY STRIP ============ -->
<section id="ch41-strip" aria-label="Memory strip">
  <div class="strip">
    <h2>🧠 The one-page memory strip — Chapter 41 in your pocket</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><b>Three classes:</b> laboratory (calibration/testing), therapeutic (symptoms + oxygenation), anesthetic (with O<sub>2</sub> for surgery).</li>
      <li><b>O<sub>2</sub>:</b> 1.429 g/L, slightly heavier than air (1.29); nonflammable but accelerates combustion; only 3.3 mL dissolves in 100 mL water.</li>
      <li><b>Air:</b> 20.95% O<sub>2</sub>, 78.1% N<sub>2</sub>, ~1% trace; 1.29 g/L. <b>CO<sub>2</sub>:</b> sp. gr. 1.52, does not support combustion, FDA 99%.</li>
      <li><b>Helium:</b> 0.1785 g/L, ≥99% pure, always with ≥20% O<sub>2</sub>; heliox = laminar flow through tight airways.</li>
      <li><b>NO:</b> toxic, supports combustion, methemoglobinemia risk; FDA: term/near-term infants, hypoxic respiratory failure, PPHN. <b>N<sub>2</sub>O:</b> sweet, anesthetic, neuropathy + fetal risks.</li>
      <li><b>Made:</b> fractional distillation (commonest, cheapest) — filter, liquefy (Joule–Thompson), boil off nitrogen. Sieves + concentrators for small concentrated amounts.</li>
      <li><b>Cylinders:</b> seamless steel; DOT 3A carbon steel, 3AA alloy; shoulder stamp = size, filling pressure, serial, owner, maker; tested every 5 or 10 years at 5/3 service pressure.</li>
      <li><b>Relief valves:</b> frangible disk (pressure), fusible plug (temperature), spring-loaded (set pressure).</li>
      <li><b>Fill:</b> service pressure at 70°F (+10% if approved); liquids by filling density. <b>Measure:</b> gas by pressure, liquid by weight.</li>
      <li><b>Duration:</b> factor = ft³ × 28.3 ÷ full psig; minutes = psig × factor ÷ flow. Liquid: 1 L = 2.5 lb → 860 L; minutes = liters ÷ flow.</li>
      <li><b>Store:</b> racks/chains, away from combustibles and heat, &lt;125°F (52°C), flammables apart from oxidizers, caps on, full apart from empty, ventilated drained 1-hour enclosure, sign readable at 5 ft (1.5 m).</li>
      <li><b>Move/use:</b> secured carts, caps on, no drop/drag/roll, labeled only; crack before the bedside, nobody in front; no oil or grease anywhere; ASSS for H/G, PISS for E; No Smoking with O<sub>2</sub> in use.</li>
      <li><b>Bulk:</b> ≥20,000 ft³; three systems (manifold, cylinder-with-reserve, bulk-with-reserve); failure = life threatening → second stand tank or manifold + portable cylinders and bag-masks to the bedside.</li>
      <li><b>Deliver:</b> 50 psi working pressure; main alarm; zone valves for maintenance/fire. ASSS large, PISS small (2-5 O<sub>2</sub>, 1-5 air), DISS low-pressure. Quick-connect: one shape per gas, never fits another.</li>
      <li><b>Meters:</b> restrictor = cheapest fixed orifice, V = (P1−P2)÷R. Bourdon = transport (not gravity dependent), wrong when distal pressure changes. Integrated = alerts under 15 min. Thorpe = true flow on 50 psig, gravity dependent; compensated (50-psig calibration, valve after tube) beats back pressure; uncompensated (atmospheric calibration, valve before tube) does not.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

